From: beitlab Robotics MilkV duo OS <image/patches>
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] rtos_cmdqu: do not kfree an uninitialized pointer in SEND_WAIT

Local fix, not from upstream.

cvi_rtos_cmdqu_ioctl() declares `wait_list` without an initializer and the
RTOS_CMDQU_SEND_WAIT case calls kfree(wait_list) twice (on copy_from_user
failure and after copy_to_user). Nothing in that case assigns it, so the
kernel frees whatever the stack held. rtos_cmdqu_send_wait() already frees
its own list entry. Initializing the pointer to NULL makes both kfree()
calls no-ops and leaves every other path unchanged.

The playground's host_ping (examples/platformio/mailbox_ping/host_ping.c)
is a userspace caller of RTOS_CMDQU_SEND_WAIT.
---
diff --git a/osdrv/interdrv/rtos_cmdqu/rtos_cmdqu.c b/osdrv/interdrv/rtos_cmdqu/rtos_cmdqu.c
index 66dfc699..6733ca7d 100644
--- a/osdrv/interdrv/rtos_cmdqu/rtos_cmdqu.c
+++ b/osdrv/interdrv/rtos_cmdqu/rtos_cmdqu.c
@@ -456,7 +456,7 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL(rtos_cmdqu_send_wait);
 static long cvi_rtos_cmdqu_ioctl(struct file *filp, unsigned int cmd, unsigned long  arg)
 {
 	struct cvi_rtos_cmdqu_device *dev = filp->private_data;
-	struct rtos_cmdqu_wait_list_t *wait_list;
+	struct rtos_cmdqu_wait_list_t *wait_list = NULL;
 	struct list_head *pos;
 	long ret = 0;
 	unsigned long flags;
